config PEIOS_PNP
	bool "PNP — Peios Network Policy packet engine"
	depends on SECURITY_PKM
	depends on NETFILTER
	depends on NETFILTER_INGRESS
	depends on NETFILTER_EGRESS
	depends on NF_CONNTRACK=y
	help
	  The Peios Network Policy packet engine: the packet and RawPacket
	  rules layers, standing at the netfilter device seats (ingress,
	  egress) and the IP hooks. Policy is a forest of rule trees read
	  from the registry; semantics live in the pnp-core Rust crate,
	  staged into security/pkm and reached over the C ABI.

	  This replaces nf_tables and the xtables family on Peios — the
	  policy frontends are configured out, the netfilter hook framework
	  and conntrack machinery stay. Until the first policy generation
	  ingests, the engine is loudly permissive (generation 0).

	  conntrack must be built-in (=y): PNP itself is built-in and reads
	  flow facts on the packet path.

	  If unsure, say N.

config PEIOS_PNP_KUNIT
	bool "PNP KUnit tests"
	depends on PEIOS_PNP && KUNIT
	default SECURITY_PKM_KUNIT
	help
	  In-kernel tests for PNP's kernel-resident glue: the seat snapshot
	  builder and the dispatch predicate. Pure rules-engine semantics
	  remain owned by the pnp-core cargo suite.
